  "worked_solution": "We have the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/4a7ae067ef93ac29b82bbe49571cf389a78b6c0afefda43651044bfe374a733a.png)\n\nSince $M$ is the midpoint of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$, the two segments $\\overset{―}{PM}$ and $\\overset{―}{MQ}$ have the same length. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PM & =MQ \\\\ 3x+1 & =x+3 \\\\ 3x+1-x & =x+3-x \\\\ 2x+1 & =3 \\\\ 2x+1-1 & =3-1 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=1\\,\\text{cm}.$",
